"--- equation-from-graph · seed 1 · difficulty 1
prompt   Write the right side of y = from this graph.
display  coordinate-plane x -4..4/1 y -4..4/1 points [] lines [(0, −2)→(1, −1)] "Coordinate plane, x-axis −4 to 4 by 1; y-axis −4 to 4 by 1; line 1 through (0, −2) and (1, −1)" [equation-from-graph]
answer   expression x-2 (x, expanded, degree 1)
input    expression
hint     Read the slope and y-intercept, then write mx + b.
step 1   Read the slope from the line.   [m = 1]
step 2   Read where the line crosses y.   [b = −2]
step 3   Combine them as mx + b.   [y = x−2]
miss     slope-intercept-swapped = -2x+1   The x coefficient is the slope; the constant is the y-intercept.
miss     intercept-sign-reversed = x+2   Read the y-intercept sign where the line crosses the vertical axis.

