"--- parallel-perpendicular · seed 1 · difficulty 1
prompt   What is the slope of a parallel line?
display  coordinate-plane x -4..4/1 y -4..4/1 points [] lines [(1, 2)→(4, 4)] "Coordinate plane, x-axis −4 to 4 by 1; y-axis −4 to 4 by 1; line 1 through (1, 2) and (4, 4)" [parallel-perpendicular parallel]
answer   exact 2/3
input    keypad
keypad   allowFraction=true allowNegative=true
hint     Parallel lines have equal slopes.
step 1   Read the reference slope.   [m = 2/3]
step 2   Parallel lines keep that slope.   [parallel slope = 2/3]
miss     negative-reciprocal-for-parallel = -1.5   Parallel lines keep the same slope; use the negative reciprocal for perpendicular lines.

--- parallel-perpendicular · seed 12345 · difficulty 1
