display  coordinate-plane x -5..5/1 y -5..5/1 points [(−4, 0), (−2, 1)] lines [] "Coordinate plane, x-axis −5 to 5 by 1; y-axis −5 to 5 by 1; points (−4, 0) and (−2, 1)" [slope-from-points]
answer   exact 1/2
input    keypad
keypad   allowFraction=true allowNegative=true
hint     Keep the point order consistent and divide rise by run.
step 1   Subtract y-values in one point order.   [1 − 0 = 1]
step 2   Subtract x-values in that order too.   [−2 − −4 = 2]
step 3   Divide rise by run and reduce.   [1/2 = 1/2]
miss     inconsistent-subtraction-order = -0.5   Subtract both coordinate pairs in the same point order.
miss     run-over-rise = 2   Slope is vertical change over horizontal change: rise over run.

