"--- slope-intercept · seed 1 · difficulty 1
prompt   What is the slope?
display  coordinate-plane x -4..4/1 y -4..4/1 points [] lines [(0, −2)→(1, −1)] "Coordinate plane, x-axis −4 to 4 by 1; y-axis −4 to 4 by 1; line 1 through (0, −2) and (1, −1)" [slope-intercept slope 1 intercept -2 y = x − 2 ask slope]
answer   exact 1/1
input    keypad
keypad   allowNegative=true
hint     Read the coefficient of x in y = mx + b.
step 1   Find the coefficient attached to x.   [m = 1]
step 2   The coefficient is the slope.   [slope = 1]
miss     intercept-as-slope = -2   The slope is the x coefficient; the constant is the y-intercept.

