exports[`recorded output: table-to-graph > matches the wording recorded when the skill landed 1`] = `
"--- table-to-graph · seed 1 · difficulty 1
prompt   Plot the highlighted table row.
display  coordinate-plane x -4..4/1 y -4..4/1 points [(2, 0), (3, 1)] lines [] "Coordinate plane, x-axis −4 to 4 by 1; y-axis −4 to 4 by 1; points (2, 0) and (3, 1)" [table-to-graph rows [(2, 0), (3, 1), (4, 2)] target-x 4]
answer   point (4, 2)
input    coordinate-plane
hint     Read both values across the highlighted row before plotting.
step 1   Find the highlighted x-value.   [x = 4]
step 2   Pair it with y from the same row.   [y = 2]
step 3   Plot x across, then y vertically.   [(4, 2)]
miss     table-coordinate-order-reversed = (2, 4)   The x column gives horizontal position and the y column gives vertical position.

